5,1,1,talk,Servas,,We must look beyond the pitch. Who actually holds the skills to execute this work?,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Asuka,,I am concerned about the gap between our success stories and actual customer retention. We need to verify which past investments truly held their users.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Minako,,I am worried about our cash reserves. We need to understand the true cost of follow-on calls and what we can borrow against.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Mio,,I’m curious about the people! Who can we actually find right now? I want to see who has time to help our new companies.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Toshio,,I want to understand why past projects stalled. I need to see the delivery records of our two holdings to find the real bottlenecks.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Servas,,"Asuka, your caution is wise. Yet without skilled hands, even perfect funding is just paper. Let us ensure the people are truly there.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Asuka,,"Servas, execution is vital, but retention is the truth. If customers leave, skills are irrelevant. We must verify the actual user base.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Minako,,"Asuka, retention is vital, but it is a symptom. I need to know the structural cost of holding these positions. @Toshio, do your delivery records show where the cash actually bled out?","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Mio,,"@Minako, I hear you! But people are the real engine. @Toshio, do your records show if we just ran out of hands to finish the work?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Minako, the records show external dependencies, not cash bleed. @Mio, it was not a lack of hands, but a lack of control over the environment.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Servas,,"Toshio, your insight is profound. We must value the hands that remain. Let us ensure the people are truly there to execute.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Asuka,,"Toshio, external dependencies explain the delay, not the churn. I need to know if the customers stayed after the product finally shipped.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Minako,,"@Toshio, external dependencies delay the work, but they do not explain the cash drain. I need to see the structural cost of holding these positions.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, that makes sense! But if the environment is tricky, we need people who know how to navigate it. I’m worried we won’t find them in time!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, the environment is the variable. We must identify which external forces stall the work before we commit capital.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
